From cbb1c0f7af55703c1715b73d9d2abba4b1b09c1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shawn Lin <shawn.lin@rock-chips.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 14:52:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 0412/1368] pmdomain: rockchip: fix clock leak on domain probe
 failure

commit d8b3847770661b7109146e6479eeadcdab9cecf0 upstream.

When of_clk_get() failed in the middle of the loop, the references of
the clocks acquired so far were leaked instead of being released by
the error path.

Fixes: d909072d0521 ("soc: rockchip: power-domain: use clk_bulk APIs")
Signed-off-by: Shawn Lin <shawn.lin@rock-chips.com>
Reviewed-by: Sebastian Reichel <sebastian.reichel@collabora.com>
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Ulf Hansson <ulfh@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman <gregkh@linuxfoundation.org>
---
 drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c b/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c
index 69ecbfa2e80f..75574aec51a1 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c
@@ -734,7 +734,7 @@ static int rockchip_pm_add_one_domain(struct rockchip_pmu *pmu,
 			dev_err(pmu->dev,
 				"%pOFn: failed to get clk at index %d: %d\n",
 				node, i, error);
-			return error;
+			goto err_put_clocks;
 		}
 	}
 
